            <ArticleTitle>Right coronary artery aneurysm with aneurysmal dilation and thrombosis of the sinoatrial nodal branch mimicking a right atrial mass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>85-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jcct.2013.12.015</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1934-5925(14)00012-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aneurysms of the branches of the coronary arteries are rare. We report a case of a right coronary artery aneurysm with aneurysmal dilation and thrombosis of the sinoatrial nodal branch presenting as a right atrial mass. The patient underwent multiple imaging evaluations before coronary CT angiography diagnosed aneurysm and thrombosis of the sinoatrial nodal branch.</AbstractText>
